  "body": "R3 could emit incorrect Part 2 component-transform metadata, admit entropy/network storage too late, and let retired network work affect a replacement connection. These repairs preserve exact high-precision samples, account for overlapping buffers before allocation, and join captured HTTP/HTTPS request owners and prevent retired WebSocket cleanup from affecting replacement connections.\n\nHTTPS now uses portable URLSession delegate streaming on Darwin and FoundationNetworking, replacing an API unavailable in the Linux toolchains. The accumulator checks exposed headers, callback data, growth and final output-copy overlap; opaque Foundation/TLS buffers remain outside its preallocation control. Its serial callback queue explicitly shares the deadline timer's service class. Two compiler-sensitive test expressions now use typed expected arrays with identical assertions. The HTTP and WebSocket held-peer fixtures no longer expire their own sockets after an incidental one-second idle period; size-limit checks require the intended error, and lifecycle barriers propagate startup failures. Actual request deadlines and suite concurrency remain unchanged.\n\nThe broader R3 changes correct signed-limb Part 2 signalling, bound packet/header work, share JPIP transfer budgets across setup and repeated requests, and report reconstruction/verification costs. Worker results use an explicit locked handoff, HTTP delimiter scanning advances linearly, and CLI host normalisation prevents the reproduced optional-URL crash. Test subprocess helpers use dedicated workers and the active CLI build.\n\nCandidate15 local validation on Apple Swift 6.4 / macOS 27.0.1 / arm64:\n\n- Full ordinary concurrency passed 1,034 XCTest cases and 324 Swift Testing declarations. Independent reconciliation matches all 1,358 discovered declarations, 38 parameterised declarations and 406 argument starts.\n- Complete partitioned AddressSanitizer and ThreadSanitizer each passed the 647-declaration JPIP target and its 711-declaration complement, with the exact full inventory and argument union. No skips or sanitizer findings occurred. This is complete partitioned coverage; a fully concurrent cross-target sanitizer pass is not claimed.\n- Release CLI14 build and all 246 process checks are retained through verified equality of all 512 applicable production/package/script/fixture inputs in15.\n- The two-volume before/after SwiftJ2K measurements retain the documented safety trade-off: median HT encode cost increased approximately 8–18%. Raw distributions, profiles and unexplained transcode tails remain visible. The measured codec files are unchanged; the new transport policy is outside that benchmark scope. No speed or compression comparison with Kakadu is claimed.\n\n`JPIPTransport.close()` is explicitly async to await captured HTTP/HTTPS owners and invoke WebSocket disconnect; terminal WebSocket reader/timeout callbacks may finish later. Isolated synchronous callers or method references may need updating. HTTP completion covers finite I/O and locked result publication, not physical thread exit; DNS can delay it. URLProtocol/scripted tests do not establish real TLS or independent peer compatibility. Shared contracts, dependencies, Swift tools floor and Apple OS minima remain unchanged.\n\nThe first hosted run 41186617163 failed before runtime testing because of the unavailable Linux API and the two macOS test expressions. Its complete job logs and missing-evidence report remain preserved, along with earlier local failures and diagnostic limitations. The failed AddressSanitizer14 WebSocket barrier cases are retained; test-only15 fixes the remaining peer expiry and labels every unchanged barrier. A new exact-head run is required after this update is published; local macOS27 results do not qualify hosted macOS26 or Linux.\n\nThis PR remains a draft and R3 remains NOT ACCEPTED. Five required independent gates are unexecuted and unwaived: combined Part10+15, native3D JPIP, the exact repository WebSocket extension, direct full38 Part2 synthesis/output, and multiple transmitted nonempty HT sets. Shared-core Kakadu refinement and the signed-limb diagnostic provide narrower evidence. Merge and R4 activation remain gated.\n\nEvidence at commit `f3c63e3df67ddf69cfaccd559e3581ea8eacdfbe`: [status](https://github.com/raster-labs/SwiftJ2K/blob/f3c63e3df67ddf69cfaccd559e3581ea8eacdfbe/Documentation/Engineering/Remediation/STATUS.md), [capability matrix](https://github.com/raster-labs/SwiftJ2K/blob/f3c63e3df67ddf69cfaccd559e3581ea8eacdfbe/Documentation/Engineering/Remediation/R3_CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md), [original evidence index](https://github.com/raster-labs/SwiftJ2K/blob/f3c63e3df67ddf69cfaccd559e3581ea8eacdfbe/Documentation/Engineering/Remediation/Evidence/R3/codex-takeover/generated-index.json), [supplemental evidence index](https://github.com/raster-labs/SwiftJ2K/blob/f3c63e3df67ddf69cfaccd559e3581ea8eacdfbe/Documentation/Engineering/Remediation/Evidence/R3/codex-takeover/ci-repair-09/indexes/b05cc28b4195a726a1fe2101ddfebeefb43b923e9a48f03f811ca5440de07c42.json), and [preserved first hosted run](https://github.com/raster-labs/SwiftJ2K/actions/runs/41186617163). The new exact-head hosted run is pending review.\n",
